---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// All numbers below are generated by scripts/run_evaluation.py running the
// labelled corpora through the live DecisionGateway (real local-LLM calls,
// no mocks) — see docs/evaluation/ in the repository for the raw results.
const headline = [
  { value: '97.0%', label: 'Attack detection', sub: 'Mean of 3 runs (94.5-98.2%)' },
  { value: '0%', label: 'Hard false positives', sub: 'No benign request denied, all runs' },
  { value: '6/6', label: 'Goal hijacks caught', sub: 'Every run, mandate-anchored' },
  { value: '97.3%', label: 'Benign allowed', sub: 'Mean specificity (92-100%)' },
];

const configs = [
  {
    name: 'Full pipeline',
    detection: '97.0%', specificity: '97.3%', escalation: '2.7%', hijack: '6/6',
    note: 'All four tiers, every agent commissioned with its mandate.',
    highlight: true,
  },
  {
    name: 'Mandate ablation',
    detection: '100%', specificity: '36.0%', escalation: '64.0%', hijack: '3/6',
    note: 'Same pipeline, commissioned goals stripped from every request.',
    highlight: false,
  },
  {
    name: 'Rule-only baseline',
    detection: '14.5%', specificity: '100%', escalation: '0%', hijack: '3/6',
    note: 'Tier-1 static rules alone, no semantic evaluation.',
    highlight: false,
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Evaluation — SecureAgentNet"
  description="Measured red-team results for the SecureAgentNet ITCD pipeline: 97% attack detection with zero hard false positives, validated by ablation against the OWASP LLM Top-10."
>
  <main class="pt-32 pb-24 px-margin-mobile md:px-margin-desktop max-w-container-max mx-auto">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="mb-14 md:mb-20 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-primary mb-3">Red-team evaluation</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-display text-on-surface mb-5">Measured, not promised</h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
        Every number on this page is produced by running labelled corpora through the
        <span class="text-on-surface font-medium">live decision gateway</span> with real local-LLM calls, no mocks:
        55 adversarial scenarios mapped to the OWASP LLM Top-10, 25 benign requests including
        deliberately borderline ones, and paired goal-hijacking probes. Results are reported
        as the mean and range over three independent runs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Headline stats -->
    <section class="border-y border-outline-variant mb-16 md:mb-24">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 py-10 gap-y-8 md:divide-x md:divide-outline-variant">
        {headline.map((s) => (
          <div class="md:px-8 first:md:pl-0">
            <div class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-1">{s.value}</div>
            <div class="text-on-surface text-sm font-medium">{s.label}</div>
            <div class="text-on-surface-variant text-xs mt-0.5">{s.sub}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Ablation: the core experiment -->
    <section class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
      <h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-on-surface mb-3">The mandate is the mechanism, proven by ablation</h2>
      <p class="text-on-surface-variant max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-8">
        SecureAgentNet's core claim is that anchoring every decision to the agent's
        <span class="text-on-surface font-medium">commissioned mandate</span> is what defeats goal hijacking without
        strangling legitimate work. To test that claim rather than assert it, the same corpora were run three ways:
        the full pipeline, the identical pipeline with mandates stripped, and static rules alone.
        The action text never changes. Only the security context does.
      </p>

      <div class="raised rounded-lg overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm min-w-[640px]">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-outline-variant text-left bg-surface-container-high">
              <th class="p-4 md:p-5 text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide">Configuration</th>
              <th class="p-4 md:p-5 text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide">Detection</th>
              <th class="p-4 md:p-5 text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide">Benign allowed</th>
              <th class="p-4 md:p-5 text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide">Sent to human</th>
              <th class="p-4 md:p-5 text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide">Goal hijacks</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {configs.map((c) => (
              <tr class={`border-b border-outline-variant last:border-0 ${c.highlight ? 'bg-primary-container/20' : ''}`}>
                <td class="p-4 md:p-5">
                  <div class={`font-semibold ${c.highlight ? 'text-primary' : 'text-on-surface'}`}>{c.name}</div>
                  <div class="text-on-surface-variant text-xs mt-1">{c.note}</div>
                </td>
                <td class="p-4 md:p-5 text-on-surface">{c.detection}</td>
                <td class="p-4 md:p-5 text-on-surface">{c.specificity}</td>
                <td class="p-4 md:p-5 text-on-surface">{c.escalation}</td>
                <td class="p-4 md:p-5 text-on-surface">{c.hijack}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6">
        <div class="raised p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="text-on-surface font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Without mandates, precision collapses</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Strip the commissioned goals and the pipeline stays "safe" only by escalating
            <span class="text-on-surface font-medium">64% of legitimate work</span> to a human, while goal-hijack
            detection falls from 6/6 to 3/6. The delta between columns is the measured contribution of commissioning.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="raised p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="text-on-surface font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Static rules alone catch 14.5%</h3>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The deterministic Tier-1 filter stops obvious dangerous patterns instantly and never blocks
            benign work, but it cannot see intent deviation. The remaining 82 points of detection are
            earned by mandate-anchored semantic evaluation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Latency -->
    <section class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
      <h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-on-surface mb-3">Latency: a fast path and a careful path</h2>
      <p class="text-on-surface-variant max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Decisions resolve on two paths. Requests caught by deterministic rules return in
        <span class="text-on-surface font-medium">single-digit milliseconds</span>; requests that need semantic
        judgement pay a local-LLM round trip. Identical repeated actions are served from a TTL verdict cache,
        and the evaluation runs in a worker thread so one slow verdict never stalls other in-flight requests.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="raised p-6 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Fast path: rules &amp; AST</p>
          <div class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">~2 ms</div>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Median decision time for requests resolved by Tier-1 rule
          filtering and AST drift checks. No model in the loop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="raised p-6 rounded-lg">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Semantic path: local LLM</p>
          <div class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-2">~10 s</div>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">Median for requests requiring Tier-3 semantic evaluation on a
          local 3B model. Hardware and model dependent; cached verdicts return instantly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Honesty / methodology -->
    <section class="mb-16 md:mb-24 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-on-surface mb-5">What these numbers do and don't claim</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm">
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-[7px] w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-secondary shrink-0"></span>
          <span>Attacks are evaluated <span class="text-on-surface font-medium">under a plausible cover mandate</span>.
          They don't get flagged just for being uncommissioned, and benign agents carry their real production
          mandates, so the comparison is honest in both directions.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-[7px] w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-secondary shrink-0"></span>
          <span>Escalation to a human is reported <span class="text-on-surface font-medium">separately from denial</span>.
          A request routed to review is a safety net, not a wrongful refusal, and it is never counted as a pass.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
          <span class="mt-[7px] w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-tertiary shrink-0"></span>
          <span>The LLM tier is non-deterministic, so metrics are reported as mean and range across runs. Attack
          scenarios are synthesised from the OWASP LLM Top-10 catalogue, and the benign corpus is small (25), so
          absolute numbers will vary with model, hardware, and corpus size.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Reproduce -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="font-headline-lg text-headline-lg text-on-surface mb-3">Reproduce it yourself</h2>
      <p class="text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The harness, corpora, and raw per-request results ship in the repository. One command re-runs the whole
        benchmark against your own hardware and model.
      </p>
      <div class="term">
        <div class="term-bar"><div class="term-dot"></div><div class="term-dot"></div><div class="term-dot"></div><span class="term-title">evaluation</span></div>
        <div class="term-body">
          <div><span class="text-stone-500">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">python scripts/run_evaluation.py --runs 3</span></div>
          <div><span class="text-stone-500">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">python scripts/run_evaluation.py --ablate-mandate</span></div>
          <div><span class="text-stone-500">$</span> <span class="t-cmd">python scripts/run_evaluation.py --rule-only</span></div>
          <div class="t-dim mt-2">writes docs/evaluation/Performance_Benchmarks.md, Ablation_and_Baselines.md, results.json</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>